<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  The Share Extension's App Group set: what every PROVISIONED build applies
  (clients/apple/ShareExtension, docs/os-integration.md). That is iOS, and the Mac App Store
  archive, which swaps this in over MACOS_SHARE_ENTITLEMENTS.

  Every other macOS build takes AllodiaMailShare.macOS.entitlements beside this file, which reaches
  a directory under the user's home instead, and carries the measurement that forced the split: a
  sandboxed process cannot use an App Group its profile did not grant, and a macOS build outside
  the Store has no profile.

  Two keys, and no third. Apple's guidance for an embedded executable is that surplus entitlements
  cause launch failures, and this one reads item providers and writes into one directory.
-->
<dict>
    <!-- macOS will not load an app extension that is not sandboxed, and the Store rejects any
         executable in a submission that is not (ITMS-90296). Both are satisfied here. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>

    <!-- The container the drop box lives in, and the only place this process and the app can both
         write (MailcalShareBox/ShareBox.swift). It must name the group the APP carries, so it is
         built from $(MAILCAL_HOST_APP_ID), a build setting project.yml gives this target from the
         brand. $(PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER), which the app's own entitlements use, would resolve
         here to the EXTENSION's id and name a group nobody else is in: the extension would launch,
         write, and be the only reader of what it wrote.

         No team-id prefix, matching the app (measured 2026-08-03). `ShareBox.entitledGroup` reads
         the running signature rather than trusting a constant, so a build given a different form
         still finds its own group, and a build given none falls back rather than failing. -->
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>group.$(MAILCAL_HOST_APP_ID)</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
